{
  "caveats": [
    "Software proxy, not a physical unplug: the NVLink bridge was never removed. The 'no bridge' arm closes both peer-to-peer paths in software (NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=1 and vLLM --disable-custom-all-reduce); a pair without a bridge has no CUDA peer-to-peer at all on consumer Ampere, which makes this a fair proxy, but a physical A/B could still differ.",
    "Dense = 1 pass: one run per arm, no repetition and no confidence interval; the noise floor is read from the middle arm, which should equal the bridged arm on the decode path.",
    "One model and one shape: a dense model all-reduces on every layer.",
    "Cold-start times are not comparable between arms (NCCL_DEBUG=INFO, CUDA graph capture, and the first arm compiled into an empty cache) and are not reported here.",
    "VRAM is what vLLM reserved (gpu-memory-utilization), not what the model needs."
  ],
