  "title": "NVLink bridge on or off (software proxy): a dense 27B in tensor parallel 2",
  "verdict": "Closing both peer-to-peer paths cost 10.1 % of single-stream speed and 22.1 % of eight-request throughput. Disabling NCCL peer-to-peer alone moved them by -0.3 % and -1.3 %, within noise: vLLM's custom all-reduce keeps using the bridge, so that experiment alone is a false negative. Time to first token did not move. The bridge changes speed, not what fits."
}
